From 868a1d0cf0db84388f60ca3114c9087c825425d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 21:53:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [ROCm] Support ROCm 10.1 (HIP 7.x) on Linux and Windows

ROCm discovery
- FindROCM.cmake: root is USE_ROCM=<path>, then ROCM_PATH, then HIP_PATH (empty values
  count as unset), then the root of hipconfig/amdclang on PATH, then /opt/rocm (not on
  Windows). Search lib and lib64. Drop the pre-3.7 hip_hcc fallback and the HSA library.
- tvm.support.rocm: same order for find_rocm_path() without shelling out to `which`.
  find_lld() prefers the ROCm linker (LLVM_PATH, <root>/lib/llvm/bin) and finds ld.lld.exe.
- tvm.support.utils.which() uses shutil.which, so Windows executable suffixes work.

Device libraries
- Bitcode is found via HIP_DEVICE_LIB_PATH, <root>/lib/llvm/amdgcn/bitcode (ROCm 7+ and
  TheRock), <root>/amdgcn/bitcode (ROCm 3.9 to 6.x) or the clang resource dir.
- BuildAMDGPU passes mcpu and thread_warp_size to tvm_callback_rocm_bitcode_path. The
  callback links ocml plus exactly one oclc_* control library per setting:
  oclc_isa_version_<gfx> for the target (previously the first of a fixed
  803/900/906/1030 list, so every GPU got gfx803's ISA constants), oclc_wavefrontsize64_on
  or _off to match the wave size, and oclc_abi_version_500. oclc_daz_opt_* and
  oclc_correctly_rounded_sqrt_*, removed in ROCm 7, are optional; irif is gone.

Target
- Use the amdgcn-amd-amdhsa triple; amdgcn-amd-amdhsa-hcc is accepted and rewritten.
- thread_warp_size has no fixed default of 64 any more: it comes from the device when the
  arch is auto-detected, else from the arch (32 on gfx10+, 64 on gfx9 and older). Wave64 on
  RDNA adds +wavefrontsize64 so LLVM generates matching code; wave32 on gfx9 is rejected.
- Drop the pre-ROCm-3.5 -code-object-v3 path.

Runtime
- kExist uses hipGetDeviceCount instead of hsa_init/hsa_shut_down, so the runtime no
  longer depends on the HSA runtime (which does not exist on Windows).
- Windows: the AMD display driver installs its own amdhip64_*.dll into System32, which the
  DLL search order prefers over PATH. libtvm_runtime_rocm and libtvm_runtime_extra now
  delay-load the ROCm DLLs and resolve them by full path from <ROCm root>\bin
  (rocm_dll_loader_win.cc). They fail instead of falling back to another copy. Python
  preloads the same DLL before loading the TVM runtime libraries.

hipBLAS
- Port to the hipDataType/hipblasComputeType_t API. hipblasDatatype_t was removed in
  hipBLAS 3 (ROCm 7), so this file no longer compiled. HIPBLAS_V2 keeps ROCm 6 working.

rocThrust may be compiled with amdclang++ as well as hipcc.

